  "mathematical_claims": [
    "For squarefree endpoint labels m,n, the pair sign is mu((m/gcd(m,n))*(n/gcd(m,n))).",
    "The complete ordered endpoint cross is the finite signed ray sum sum_{q>=2} mu(q)*W_T(q), with W_T(q)>=0.",
    "At T=log 12, q=11 and primes 2,3,5, the exact third multiplicative difference equals 8*A*B with A<0 and B>0.",
    "Therefore the exact ray weights are not third-order completely monotone.",
    "The counterexample is caused by literal un-birthed cutoff faces and blocks an unsigned Euler-product or positive-measure parity bootstrap."
  ],
